.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Helmholtz (1868) and Kelvin (1871) showed that any interface between two fluid layers sliding past each other is unconditionally unstable: the shear itself supplies the energy to grow a small ripple, with no velocity threshold required. kelvin_helmholtz_ic seeds exactly this thin, rippled shear layer as a vorticity field on a doubly periodic domain, and NavierStokes2D evolves it by integrating the 2D incompressible vorticity-transport equation">

